**Why two changes:**

1. `get_unpacked_marks`: For class types, instead of `getattr(obj, "pytestmark", [])` (which follows MRO and stops at the first class that has `pytestmark`, dropping markers on sibling bases), we iterate `obj.__mro__` and look up `__dict__` directly on each class, collecting markers from *all* ancestors.

2. `store_mark`: Must pass `consider_mro=False` so that when decorating a class with a mark, we don't flatten inherited marks into the class's own `pytestmark` attribute — if we did, every child class would redundantly re-own all ancestor marks and they'd be collected again when `get_unpacked_marks` iterates the MRO.

